19. checking the type of characters

Python provides several useful methods for character classification.

Method                      Returns TRUE value when
isalpha()                   All characters are alphabetic and string is non empty
isdigit()                   All characters are digits and string is non empty
isalnum()                   All characters are alphabetic or numeric and string is non empty
isspace()                   all characters are white spaces and string is non empty
islower()                   there is at least one cased character and all cased characters are lowercase
isupper()                   there is at least one cased character and all cased characters are uppercase
istitle()                   The string follows python's title-case rules.

code:

print("Python".isalpha()) #true
print("12345".isdigit()) #true
print("Python123".isalnum()) #true
print(" ".isspace()) #true
print("hello".islower()) #true
print("HELLO".isupper()) #true

this works differently. although 12345 is number but we have enclosed in double commas.
print(12345.isdigit()) #this raise a Syntax error

these methods return boolean values true or false.

